# E28 -- Which lever keeps a pack together? CTRL with only dingo, kangaroo and wombat allowed, coupling on with packs of seven and ecology off: the first prey group's coupling brings a dingo pack of seven. Four arms, applied every 1,500 ticks to every wild dingo: control (nothing); a shared station (idle_area at the pack's first centroid, threshold 8, WildernessRoamer); a leader (the lowest-id dingo, the rest following it at distance 4 as PACK_LEADER); a centroid nudge (any dingo more than 8 tiles from the centroid teleported to within 4 of it). Mean Chebyshev distance to the centroid per sample, from units.tsv, is the measure. Thirty thousand ticks, two replicates each.
run 20260917-214221 fort CTRL backup CTRL.preverify
DF v0.53.16 win64 STEAM DFHack 53.16-r1.1 world The Legendary Dimension site 32 tiles 29..29,20..20 seed WILDERPOP1
